@@ -12,6 +12,9 @@ The format of this change log follows the advice given at [Keep a CHANGELOG](htt
 
 #### Added
 
+- A standard PHP API for mounting React components has been added. `\core\output\html_writer::react_component()` generates the mount point for a React component from the component identifier and its props, handling prop serialisation and escaping. Renderables can also implement the new `\core\output\react_component_renderable` interface, which is rendered as a React mount point by `render()`. It takes precedence over `named_templatable`, and a `render_[renderable]` method on the renderer takes precedence over it.
+
+  For more information see [MDL-89296](https://tracker.moodle.org/browse/MDL-89296)
 - `email_to_user()` now emits a hook `before_email_to_user`. This hook allows any subscriber to modify the email contents, add additional headers, or add reasons to block the email. If any block reasons are added, the email is stopped from being sent and the reasons are output.
 
   For more information see [MDL-69724](https://tracker.moodle.org/browse/MDL-69724)
